Package: akari
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         python3 (>= 3.13),
         python3-fastapi,
         python3-uvicorn,
         python3-websockets (>= 15),
         python3-httpx,
         python3-multipart,
         python3-pil,
         python3-pampy,
         libpam-systemd,
         dbus-user-session,
         systemd,
         passwd,
         procps,
         iproute2,
         sudo,
         openssh-server,
         caddy,
         qrencode,
         libjs-xterm,
         novnc
Recommends: akari-shell, unattended-upgrades
Description: desktop in the browser for a Linux machine (akarid)
 Akari OS puts a desktop in the browser on top of a Debian system: windows,
 a terminal, files, music and Linux apps (each in its own Xvnc, shown with
 noVNC), for every account of the machine.
 .
 This package has akarid, the system service that signs accounts in with
 PAM and starts their sessions (akari-session@.service, with a logind
 session each), the session agent, the web interface, and the HTTPS front
 (a Caddy configuration with its own certificate).

