            qemu-guest-agent,
            open-vm-tools,
            hyperv-daemons
Description: Akari OS desktop: akari with its apps, fonts and cursors
 Everything a machine needs to be an Akari OS desktop: akari and
 akari-shell, the display stack for Linux apps (TigerVNC, matchbox),
 Firefox ESR, fonts with CJK, network tools, and the guest tools for
 QEMU/KVM, VMware and Hyper-V, which only start on their own hypervisor.
 .
 It also has the Akari cursor theme for X, made from the same pictures the
 browser shows, and makes it the default.

Package: akari-role-container
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         docker.io,
         docker-compose
Description: Akari OS server role: Container-Host (Docker and Compose)
 A server role, added and taken away in Akari's Server-Manager: Docker from
 Debian with Compose, managed in Akari's Docker app. Taking the role away
 stops Docker; images, volumes and containers stay in /var/lib/docker.

Package: akari-role-files
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         samba,
         wsdd2
Description: Akari OS server role: Dateiserver (Samba)
 A server role, added and taken away in Akari's Server-Manager: Samba to
 share folders with Windows, macOS and Linux, and wsdd2 so that Windows finds
 the machine in its network. Taking the role away keeps the folders and
 /etc/samba.

Package: akari-server
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         btop,
         ncdu,
         tmux,
         rsync,
         jq,
         lsof,
         iotop,
         sysstat,
         smartmontools,
         lm-sensors,
         ethtool,
         fail2ban,
         systemd-zram-generator,
         unattended-upgrades
Description: Akari OS as a server: tools and settings for a machine that serves
 The tools a server wants at hand: btop, ncdu, tmux, rsync, jq, lsof, iotop,
 sysstat, smartmontools, lm-sensors and ethtool.
 .
 And the settings: fail2ban shuts out whoever guesses SSH passwords; swap in
 compressed RAM (zram) before any disk; TCP with BBR and fair queueing; a
 journal that survives restarts (at most 1 GB, a month); no suspend or
 hibernation, also not when a laptop's lid closes. All of them are files of
 their own, in /usr/lib where systemd allows it, so a file of the same name in
 /etc overrides them.

Package: akari-shell
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends},
         zsh,
         zsh-autosuggestions,
         zsh-syntax-highlighting,
         fastfetch,
         fontconfig,
         kmscon
Description: zsh as Akari OS sets it up: oh-my-zsh, powerlevel10k, fastfetch
 The shell of Akari OS, for the terminal in the browser and for ssh:
 oh-my-zsh and powerlevel10k on fixed versions, read-only in /usr/share,
 with gitstatusd for git in the prompt; the font MesloLGS NF that
 powerlevel10k is made for, the Akari Symbols font, and fastfetch with the
 Akari logo in the account's accent colour.
 .
 New accounts get a ~/.zshrc that loads it (/etc/skel/.zshrc).
 .
 The console on the machine itself runs in kmscon with the same font, so
 the prompt's symbols, 256 colours and Akari's mark show there too; the
 keyboard is the system's. Where kmscon cannot run, agetty takes over.
